{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 01 - Download Sentinel-2 images of Ronti Peak (Chamoli), 2015-2021\n",
    "\n",
    "Week 2, part A of the Slope Watch project.\n",
    "\n",
    "What this notebook does:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Searches a free public catalog for Sentinel-2 scenes covering the slope.\n",
    "2. Lists the scenes and suggests one clear autumn date per year.\n",
    "3. Reads only a 5 km crop around the collapse scar from each chosen scene.\n",
    "4. Saves the crops to `data/chamoli/` with an index file.\n",
    "5. Displays them so you can check they look right.\n",
    "\n",
    "Run the cells in order. Select the project's `.venv` as the notebook kernel first."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Setup"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import rasterio\n",
    "from pystac_client import Client\n",
    "from rasterio.warp import transform_bounds\n",
    "from rasterio.windows import from_bounds\n",
    "\n",
    "# Project root: works whether the notebook runs from notebooks/ or the repo root.\n",
    "ROOT = Path.cwd() if (Path.cwd() / \".git\").exists() else Path.cwd().parent\n",
    "DATA_DIR = ROOT / \"data\" / \"chamoli\"\n",
    "DATA_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 5 km x 5 km box centred on the collapse scar (about 30.377 N, 79.731 E),\n",
    "# located on Sentinel-2 images from 31 Jan and 10 Feb 2021 in the Copernicus Browser.\n",
    "# Order: west, south, east, north (degrees).\n",
    "BBOX = [79.705, 30.355, 79.757, 30.400]\n",
    "\n",
    "CATALOG_URL = \"https://earth-search.aws.element84.com/v1\"\n",
    "COLLECTION = \"sentinel-2-l2a\"   # if 2015-2018 come back sparse, try \"sentinel-2-l1c\"\n",
    "BAND = \"red\"                    # a 10 m band; \"nir\" also works\n",
    "DATE_RANGE = \"2015-06-01/2021-02-06\"   # ends the day before the collapse\n",
    "MAX_CLOUD = 20                  # percent, for the whole scene\n",
    "print(\"Saving to:\", DATA_DIR)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Search the catalog"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "catalog = Client.open(CATALOG_URL)\n",
    "search = catalog.search(\n",
    "    collections=[COLLECTION],\n",
    "    bbox=BBOX,\n",
    "    datetime=DATE_RANGE,\n",
    "    query={\"eo:cloud_cover\": {\"lt\": MAX_CLOUD}},\n",
    ")\n",
    "items = list(search.items())\n",
    "print(len(items), \"scenes found\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Check the band names once; BAND above must be one of these.\n",
    "if items:\n",
    "    print(\"Available assets:\", sorted(items[0].assets.keys()))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. List the scenes and suggest dates\n",
    "\n",
    "The table shows every scene. The suggestion keeps October and November only\n",
    "(little snow, similar sun angle each year) and picks the least cloudy scene per year.\n",
    "\n",
    "The cloud figure is for the whole 100 km scene, so it can be wrong for the slope itself.\n",
    "Check each suggested date in the Copernicus Browser before trusting it."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "scenes = pd.DataFrame(\n",
    "    {\n",
    "        \"date\": [it.datetime.date() for it in items],\n",
    "        \"cloud\": [it.properties.get(\"eo:cloud_cover\") for it in items],\n",
    "        \"id\": [it.id for it in items],\n",
    "    }\n",
    ").sort_values(\"date\").reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "scenes[\"year\"] = pd.to_datetime(scenes[\"date\"]).dt.year\n",
    "scenes[\"month\"] = pd.to_datetime(scenes[\"date\"]).dt.month\n",
    "\n",
    "print(scenes.groupby(\"year\").size().rename(\"scenes per year\"))\n",
    "scenes"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "autumn = scenes[scenes[\"month\"].isin([10, 11])]\n",
    "suggested = autumn.sort_values(\"cloud\").groupby(\"year\").head(2).sort_values(\"date\")\n",
    "suggested[[\"date\", \"cloud\", \"id\"]]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Choose the dates\n",
    "\n",
    "Edit `CHOSEN_IDS` to the scenes you want (10 to 15 is a good number).\n",
    "It starts as the suggestion from the cell above."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "CHOSEN_IDS = list(suggested[\"id\"])   # replace with your own list of ids if you prefer\n",
    "\n",
    "chosen_items = [it for it in items if it.id in set(CHOSEN_IDS)]\n",
    "chosen_items.sort(key=lambda it: it.datetime)\n",
    "print(len(chosen_items), \"scenes chosen\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Read only the crop from each scene"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def read_crop(item, bbox=BBOX, band=BAND):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Read just the bbox window of one band from a scene, without downloading the whole file.\"\"\"\n",
    "    with rasterio.open(item.assets[band].href) as src:\n",
    "        box = transform_bounds(\"EPSG:4326\", src.crs, *bbox)\n",
    "        window = from_bounds(*box, transform=src.transform)\n",
    "        return src.read(1, window=window).astype(\"float32\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Try one first.\n",
    "test = read_crop(chosen_items[0])\n",
    "print(\"Crop shape:\", test.shape, \"| value range:\", test.min(), \"to\", test.max())\n",
    "plt.imshow(test, cmap=\"gray\")\n",
    "plt.title(str(chosen_items[0].datetime.date()))\n",
    "plt.axis(\"off\")\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Save all the crops and an index file\n",
    "\n",
    "Each crop is saved as `data/chamoli/YYYY-MM-DD.npy`.\n",
    "If two scenes share a date, the less cloudy one is kept."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "rows, seen = [], set()\n",
    "for item in sorted(chosen_items, key=lambda it: it.properties.get(\"eo:cloud_cover\", 100)):\n",
    "    date = item.datetime.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\")\n",
    "    if date in seen:\n",
    "        continue\n",
    "    seen.add(date)\n",
    "    crop = read_crop(item)\n",
    "    np.save(DATA_DIR / f\"{date}.npy\", crop)\n",
    "    rows.append(\n",
    "        {\n",
    "            \"date\": date,\n",
    "            \"cloud\": item.properties.get(\"eo:cloud_cover\"),\n",
    "            \"id\": item.id,\n",
    "            \"rows\": crop.shape[0],\n",
    "            \"cols\": crop.shape[1],\n",
    "            \"file\": f\"{date}.npy\",\n",
    "        }\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    print(\"saved\", date, crop.shape)\n",
    "\n",
    "index = pd.DataFrame(rows).sort_values(\"date\").reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "index.to_csv(DATA_DIR / \"index.csv\", index=False)\n",
    "index"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Display and check\n",
    "\n",
    "Things to look for:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Every crop has the same shape (about 500 x 500) and shows the same area.\n",
    "- The north face of Ronti Peak sits near the middle of each image.\n",
    "- No crop is mostly cloud or fresh snow. Drop any that are, and rerun from step 4."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "index = pd.read_csv(DATA_DIR / \"index.csv\")\n",
    "n = len(index)\n",
    "cols = 4\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(int(np.ceil(n / cols)), cols, figsize=(16, 4 * int(np.ceil(n / cols))))\n",
    "for ax in np.atleast_1d(axes).ravel():\n",
    "    ax.axis(\"off\")\n",
    "for ax, (_, row) in zip(np.atleast_1d(axes).ravel(), index.iterrows()):\n",
    "    img = np.load(DATA_DIR / row[\"file\"])\n",
    "    lo, hi = np.percentile(img, [2, 98])\n",
    "    ax.imshow(np.clip((img - lo) / (hi - lo + 1e-9), 0, 1), cmap=\"gray\")\n",
    "    ax.set_title(f\"{row['date']}  (cloud {row['cloud']:.0f}%)\")\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Shapes:\", sorted(set(zip(index[\"rows\"], index[\"cols\"]))))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "Contains modified Copernicus Sentinel data, accessed through the Earth Search catalog on AWS Open Data.\n",
    "\n",
    "Next: `02_testbed.ipynb` (shift a patch by a known amount, add noise and fake clouds)."
   ]
  }
 ],
